===============================================================================
DATA SHIPPED WITH THIS REPOSITORY
===============================================================================

data/teaching/flat75_025m.tif
data/teaching/flat75_4m.tif

    ⚠️ SYNTHETIC. NOT SURVEY DATA. NOT KARTVERKET. Every cell is exactly
    75.000 m — a flat plane and nothing else. They exist so the instrument opens
    without fetching anything, and so a workshop begins in the collapsed state
    and has to earn its way out. They must never be described, exported or cited
    as terrain data. See data/teaching/SOURCE.txt, which travels with them.

    Their georeference IS real — EPSG:25833 (EUREF89 UTM33N), the Ørndalen
    origins — because the biotic model is calibrated for Troms: the species
    envelopes, solar geometry at 69.7 °N and the prevailing Tromsø south-wester
    only mean anything at that location.

data/orndalen/*.tif  —  TERRAIN DATA © KARTVERKET, NLOD / CC BY 4.0

    ⚠️ ATTRIBUTION IS A LICENCE CONDITION, NOT A COURTESY. Anything derived from
    these tiles — a figure, a drawing, an export, a slide — must credit
    Kartverket. The instrument does this automatically wherever terrain is
    shown, keyed on the tile name; if you rename the tiles, check that the
    credit still appears.

    Fetched 2026-07-30 from the hoydedata.no ArcGIS ImageServer, Tromsøya 10 pkt
    2024 epoch (last flight 2024-08-07, 10 pt/m²), EPSG:25833 / NN2000. Full
